Description: Decomposes macroeconomic time series into trend and cycle with
    the Hodrick-Prescott (HP) filter and two data-driven versions of it. The
    modified HP filter of McDermott (1997), assessed by Choudhary, Hanif and
    Iqbal (2014) <doi:10.1080/00036846.2014.894631>, chooses the smoothing
    parameter of every series by generalised cross-validation (as described
    in Coe and McDermott (1997) <doi:10.2307/3867497>). The fully modified HP
    filter of Hanif, Iqbal and Choudhary (2017, State Bank of Pakistan
    Working Paper 88) also reduces the end-point bias of the HP filter: it
    raises the smoothing parameter at the first and last observations, with
    linear or quadratic weights chosen to minimise the loss of Bloechl (2014,
    University of Munich Discussion Paper 2014-1). Every filter is a banded
    linear solve, so the searches are fast; batch processing of many series,
    comparisons of the filters, the filter weights, gain functions and
    end-point loss, simulation of trend-plus-cycle series and the power
    comparison of the paper, 'ggplot2' graphics, a plain-language
    interpretation of every result and a built-in 'shiny' application.
